  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nSurface high pressure centered over the Great Lakes will move\nsoutheast through the weekend. Southerly flow will then become \nestablished early next week. Meanwhile, heights will be rising as mid\nlevel high pressure slowly translates east. This will result in dry \nconditions through at least Tuesday. Today is forecast to be the \ncoolest day with temperatures slightly below normal. There will then \nbe a warming trend with increasing dew points. Highs will get back \ninto the lower 90s next week and heat indices will rise into the mid \nto upper 90s.",
